    },
    {
      "_key": "k3",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "k4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) is a stable Core Web Vital metric for\nmeasuring perceived load speed. It marks the point in the page load timeline\nwhen the page's main content has likely loaded. A fast LCP helps reassure\nthe user that the page is useful."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "blockquote"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k5",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "k6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "- "
        },
        {
          "_key": "k8",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "k7"
          ],
          "text": "web.dev"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "k7",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://web.dev/articles/lcp"
        }
      ],
      "style": "blockquote"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k9",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "k10",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What this means is that we should target as small of an LCP as possible."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k11",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "k12",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Now, let's dive into a pretty interesting case of LCP being affected in a way that you might not expect."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k13",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "k14",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Problem"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
